21. One-Minute Interview Explanation

If an interviewer asks you to explain Parquet, say:

«"Parquet is a columnar file format designed for analytical workloads. Unlike row-oriented formats, it stores data by column, so if a query only needs a few columns, the engine doesn't have to read the entire dataset. This reduces I/O and improves performance. Parquet also supports compression and encoding, which reduce storage and data transfer. Internally, a Parquet file is organized into row groups, column chunks and pages, and it stores metadata and statistics that can help the query engine skip irrelevant data."»

That is the explanation you should be able to give without looking at notes.